# DWS standards — always follow (Cursor harness)

HIC approved 19.09.2026: thin always-on rule; migration CI; i18n HTML provenance; caller map; Auth leaked-password (Studio, Security Standard §16.0.2). Do not apply 088.

Do not "remember" standards. **Read the files.** Dumping `CLAUDE.md` is not compliance.

## Every task, before edits

1. Read `docs/system-config/STANDARDS_ROUTING.md`.
2. Read `DWS_TRUTH_STANDARD.md` and `DWS_ROLES_REGISTRY.md` (always).
3. Read **every** other standard the routing table matches (Security, Document, Brand, Learning, …).
4. In the HIC reply, one line: `Standards loaded: <paths>`. If a match was skipped: `N/A — <reason>` (Discipline Rule 12).
5. If a loaded standard has a **gap** (silent, contradictory, or missing a NIS2/Katakri/AI Act control): propose the update (field note + draft wording). Do not only N/A. See `STANDARDS_ROUTING.md` How to Apply step 4.

## Executable source (Document Standard §1 / §19.3)

New or rewritten `.sql`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.py`: language-appropriate `CODE VERSIONING NOTE` including `Harness` and `Hic-Approved-Drift` (`none` or dated HIC id). SQL filenames: `[NNN]_[DDMMYY]_[name].sql`. Never paste markdown `VERSION AND AGENT HISTORY` into source.

Narrative `.md`: `VERSION AND AGENT HISTORY` with `***` delimiters (not `---`).

## Do not

- Apply migrations / send email / publish blogs without the zone in `CLAUDE.md`.
- Invent prices, role names, or industry counts — Truth Standard first.
